  {
   "text": "No mint or other trusted parties.",
   "date": "1 Nov 2008",
   "where": "Cryptography Mailing List",
   "url": "https://satoshi.nakamotoinstitute.org/emails/cryptography/1/"
  },
  {
   "text": "Participants can be anonymous.",
   "date": "1 Nov 2008",
   "where": "Cryptography Mailing List",
   "url": "https://satoshi.nakamotoinstitute.org/emails/cryptography/1/"
  },
  {
   "text": "It's very attractive to the libertarian viewpoint if we can explain it properly.",
   "date": "13 Nov 2008",
   "where": "Cryptography Mailing List",
   "url": "https://satoshi.nakamotoinstitute.org/emails/cryptography/12/"
  },
  {
   "text": "I'm better with code than with words though.",
   "date": "13 Nov 2008",
   "where": "Cryptography Mailing List",
   "url": "https://satoshi.nakamotoinstitute.org/emails/cryptography/12/"
  },
  {
   "text": "It's completely decentralized with no server or central authority.",
   "date": "9 Jan 2009",
   "where": "Cryptography Mailing List",
   "url": "https://satoshi.nakamotoinstitute.org/emails/cryptography/16/"
  },
  {
   "text": "Total circulation will be 21,000,000 coins.",
   "date": "9 Jan 2009",
   "where": "Cryptography Mailing List",
   "url": "https://satoshi.nakamotoinstitute.org/emails/cryptography/16/"
  },
  {
   "text": "It might make sense just to get some in case it catches on.",
   "date": "17 Jan 2009",
   "where": "Cryptography Mailing List",
   "url": "https://satoshi.nakamotoinstitute.org/emails/cryptography/17/"
  },
  {
   "text": "The root problem with conventional currency is all the trust that's required to make it work.",
   "date": "11 Feb 2009",
   "where": "P2P Foundation",
   "url": "https://satoshi.nakamotoinstitute.org/posts/p2pfoundation/1/"
  },
  {
   "text": "How does everyone feel about the B symbol with the two lines through the outside?",
